{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea","id":1514713,"title":"Alternative W5 idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-12T09:48:09-07:00","id":1514713,"title":"Alternative W5 idea","content":"I've never done this to a game not yet released, but I figured since W5 is currently a disjointed mess of WtA, Forsaken and weird human focus, I'd offer a house-ruled setting that might work better.<br /> <br /> Please note, I am not saying I am a better writer than professional RPG writers. This is just how I'd see W5 working better in my mind.<br /> <br /> To wit, a strong theme of W5 is balancing being a monster with your humanity, along with the monster species you are fighting a very dire war. You are forced to choose between joining the war or keeping in touch with your humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, let us lean into that. Instead of the garou being born, they are created through a special bite. This means the PCs were humans or wolves before the Change and so they have a very good reason to cling to their touchstones.<br /> <br /> Second, we do not know if the apocalypse or the wyrm are either evil or even real. The Garou Nation says they are, but there is enough doubt that it might be just propaganda. Maybe the Nation is just trying to justify ecoterrorism and attacking rivals. Or maybe there is something to their yapping. The point is, the PCs once more have reasons to distance themselves from the Garou Nation or join in, both of which are presented as valid options.<br /> <br /> Third, each tribe represents a different take on being a werewolf and what being one means.<br /> <br /> For example;<br /> <br /> The Silver Fangs say a werewolf is destined to stand above humanity, but also to shepherd them to the right direction.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons say being a werewolf means giving up your ties to the sinful human world and embracing the animal. The tribe solely consists of those created from humans.<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers are the opposite, they say to those created from wolves to embrace the human world and its ease of living. The tribe consists of wolf born only.<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers agree that being a werewolf sucks, but you have to at least try to fix some things.<br /> <br /> The Black Spiral Dancers say that being a werewolf is freedom from human morality and laws. You are the ruler of your own destiny.<br /> <br /> And so on, the main point is that no one has the right answer.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T10:03:18-07:00","id":1514715,"title":"","content":"Why should we reinvent the wheel? <br /> I mean w20 was nice with all of its flaws... if W5 crash and burn, I presume people will go back to the one they knew and played for years - many won't even touch W5 I guess<br /> <br /> But a nice tought-experiment nonetheless, I'm curious about the ideas and solutions of other STs and players","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T11:06:33-07:00","id":1514723,"title":"","content":"Here is my half-baked contribuition.<br /> <br /> Hart Wardens: A tribe that lives divided between being a man or being a wolf and tries to find a middle ground between the two mostly becoming hunters in small villages and in suburbs close to forested areas, composed mainly of homids, but also having lupines in their numbers, usually those curious about human culture, have a low number of Metis. A newly formed tribe.<br /> <br /> Fianna: A group that has its origins coming from the country of Wales, they are a tribe very connected to enjoying everything that life and nature can offer, enjoying everything very intensely, whether their passions or their fights, since they are also part of life as as a whole, their motto is: &quot;Even in your darkest hour, Always try to find the bright side of life&quot; composed mostly by homids, with a few lupines, although a considerable amount of Metis are generated by the members of this tribe, very few are the ones who join her.<br /> <br /> Fenhrir: &quot;Barbarian&quot; wolves are believed by many to originate from Scandinavia, but today their blood is so diluted that you can hardly make any connections. Every werewolf is influenced by rage and fenrirs more than others, no tribe knows more about rage than they do, which many believe that means that they live in a constant state of rage, however the truth is that however much the Fenrir embrace their savage rage they see it not as a way of life but as a weapon, rage is part of them, to be feared but not ignored, it is part of them but not their whole. Composed of humans and lupines in almost equal proportions, strangely, they have a small share of Metis, but it is unknown if these were sired by the tribe itself, rumors that the progenitors would be executed as punishment.<br /> <br /> Wendigo: Tribe of indigeneous origin extremely linked to the spiritual side of the Garou, its members usually live in villages mostly secluded in indigenous preservation areas, which is where most homid members come from. Known for a strange coldness in moments of peace and an unrivaled ferocity in battle, the truth is that the Wendigo have no time for frivolous friendships, preferring genuine friendships and those who consider family, for a member of the Wendigo, your tribe is your family and also a inreplaceable treasure. Composed mostly of Lupines and Homids from the forest reserves, their totem accepts with MUCH difficulty outsiders, rumors that they cultivate Metis among their numbers, usually coming from Lupine parents, a rumor considered disturbing by other tribes.<br /> <br /> Ghost Council: A tribe shrouded in mystery, there are several rumors of their origin, but none confirmed, they follow their own agenda by harvesting and storing the secrets of the supernatural and share only a portion of them with a few hand-selected individuals, it is not known for sure why they do this, but some assume they are looking for a way to break the ancient curses or restore Gaia's power, but no one knows as they don't speak and this silence is frightening to the other tribes, needless to say that the mark of this tribe is distrust. It is not known the proportions or numbers of members of the tribe, but if it is assumed that you cannot enter voluntarily, you are chosen.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T11:20:29-07:00","id":1514725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1514715#post1514715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should we reinvent the wheel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a lot of people who like Werewolves did not like WtA's wheels. W5 could have been a chance to focus on the cursed-type of werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T11:43:26-07:00","id":1514726,"title":"","content":"I would say no to the 'infecting bite' idea and resulting struggle against the beast within- not because it isn't thematically fitting or a bad idea. It's just already covered by Vampire, which explores that theme in detail.<br /> <br /> To me, at it's core, Werewolf is a coming-of-age story game:<br /> - your body starts to change in weird ways<br /> - your emotions run amok<br /> - you are thrown - by birth, not by choice - into a world with strange traditions and social norms, some of which make zero sense to you<br /> - you carry a <i>ton</i> of expectations about what you should become and how you should behave and what you should believe\u200b. Your family already decided all that for you.<br /> - your elders have seriously messed the whole world up, but somehow still expect you to respect them and fix their mistakes<br /> - and all you have to do is sort it all out so you can live with it. Oh, and save the world.<br /> <br /> It's less a game of escapism and more about exploring these real-life problems from a different perspective for me. Plus you can punch the problems in the face with agg damage, for instant gratification.<br /> <br /> IMO it shouldn't be too hard to keep those key aspects and transport it to a current time setting. These things don't change much between generations, but the world does, and the question for the players is how they are going to deal with it. The setting should support 'figuring yourself out', while throwing enough problems at the player to provide something to struggle or rebel against.<br /> From the previews I have read, this is something that the W20 Tribes in my opinion did better than W5. They provided a home and identity on one hand, and came with a crapton of burdens on the other. Some of the bad stuff the Tribes had was <i>good</i>. Going back to the coming-of-age theme, growing up in a house of no troubles is nice, but doesn't provide the narrative grip it needs to go with the theme. W20 Tribes were like your more or less dysfunctional family, W5 Tribes feel - to me - more like the guys you hang out with after school. Different social function. Bottom line, the Tribes in W5 would need to be more problematic to work.<br /> <br /> Coming from a more human centered perspective and setting it all 'post-apocalypse' are not bad ideas as such. Wolves are mostly gone from the more populated parts of the world, while more people live in the denser population centers instead of out in the country; simply stating it like that would be sufficient to explain the narrower focus without excluding wolf-born completely. The ecological situation is.. well, it's really f-ing bad, isn't it? If Gaia is not already past the point of no return, she is very close. And the current generation knows it - and as terrible as it is to say this - fits like a glove to the game's premise.<br /> The 'loss of the wolf' is something that could be worked into the setting as a symbol for the losing war, and another point for players to rebel against. If the focus is more on humanity, then the antagonists should also be more human. As is evident, we do not need the help of supernatural evil to destroy our world. That's not to say that the spiritual side of the setting should vanish. Aside from pure game mechanics, it provides another possible anchor for players to ground themselves with.<br /> <br /> tldr; the setting progressions in W5 are not as much of a problem as the disappearance of narrative key elements that support the game's premise. In my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:19:43-07:00","id":1514731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1514725#post1514725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because a lot of people who like Werewolves did not like WtA's wheels. W5 could have been a chance to focus on the cursed-type of werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we need to take a step back fro this and discuss what is wanted here. I don't believe that Werewolf: The Apocalypse should be a game about the Cursed-type Werewolf. If the goal is to make a new Werewolf game, it should not be along the lines of W:tA. The idea of the Cursed Werewolf that still seeks to fight monsters is one that's quite ubiquitous in the horror and action horror genre, and it's a fruitful area to pillage. Possibly starting with things like Van Helsing, Werewolf by night and the Howling Commandoes.<br /> <br /> if the goal is to take what WtA is and refine it and reinvision it for a modern era, that's a whole other kettle of fish. My first read of your thread was that this was your goal, about how to make a fifth edition of the game we already have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:37:22-07:00","id":1514736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1514726#post1514726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say no to the 'infecting bite' idea and resulting struggle against the beast within- not because it isn't thematically fitting or a bad idea. It's just already covered by Vampire, which explores that theme in detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if that is true, WoD does not offer you a chance to even try to play a cursed shifter. This rewrite was dedicated to offer that option within the limits of WtA.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:40:15-07:00","id":1514737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1514731#post1514731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we need to take a step back fro this and discuss what is wanted here. I don't believe that Werewolf: The Apocalypse should be a game about the Cursed-type Werewolf. If the goal is to make a new Werewolf game, it should not be along the lines of W:tA. The idea of the Cursed Werewolf that still seeks to fight monsters is one that's quite ubiquitous in the horror and action horror genre, and it's a fruitful area to pillage. Possibly starting with things like Van Helsing, Werewolf by night and the Howling Commandoes.<br /> <br /> if the goal is to take what WtA is and refine it and reinvision it for a modern era, that's a whole other kettle of fish. My first read of your thread was that this was your goal, about how to make a fifth edition of the game we already have.</div> </div> </div> </div>W5 is said to be a reboot, so I figured this was one thing that could make the reboot stand on its own compared to the old versions.<br /> <br /> That and, let's be honest, what we've seen from the previews already supports this sort of gameplay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:59:19-07:00","id":1514740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1514736#post1514736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if that is true, WoD does not offer you a chance to even try to play a cursed shifter. This rewrite was dedicated to offer that option within the limits of WtA.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see. In that case the idea would need to be adapted to WtA's theme in a distinct way - the problem I have is coming up with something that is different from a Gangrel. If you want to mechanically support the struggle and inner turmoil, Vampire's Beast/Hunger/Humanity/Frenzy basis is already pretty good at doing that. Do you have something specific in mind that would distinguish a cursed shifter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:48:32-07:00","id":1514763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1514726#post1514726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, at it's core, Werewolf is a coming-of-age story game:<br /> - your body starts to change in weird ways<br /> - your emotions run amok</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically puberty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - you are thrown - by birth, not by choice - into a world with strange traditions and social norms, some of which make zero sense to you<br /> - you carry a <i>ton</i> of expectations about what you should become and how you should behave and what you should believe\u200b. Your family already decided all that for you. </div> </div> </div>Strangely it triggers me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - your elders have seriously messed the whole world up, but somehow still expect you to respect them and fix their mistakes<br /> - and all you have to do is sort it all out so you can live with it. Oh, and save the world. </div> </div> </div>Definitely not escapism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's less a game of escapism and more about exploring these real-life problems from a different perspective for me. Plus you can punch the problems in the face with agg damage, for instant gratification. </div> </div> </div>I think if you can deal aggravated damage on your problems already counts as escapism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IMO it shouldn't be too hard to keep those key aspects and transport it to a current time setting. These things don't change much between generations, but the world does, and the question for the players is how they are going to deal with it. The setting should support 'figuring yourself out', while throwing enough problems at the player to provide something to struggle or rebel against.<br /> From the previews I have read, this is something that the W20 Tribes in my opinion did better than W5. They provided a home and identity on one hand, and came with a crapton of burdens on the other. Some of the bad stuff the Tribes had was <i>good</i>. Going back to the coming-of-age theme, growing up in a house of no troubles is nice, but doesn't provide the narrative grip it needs to go with the theme. W20 Tribes were like your more or less dysfunctional family, W5 Tribes feel - to me - more like the guys you hang out with after school. Different social function. Bottom line, the Tribes in W5 would need to be more problematic to work.<br /> <br /> Coming from a more human centered perspective and setting it all 'post-apocalypse' are not bad ideas as such. Wolves are mostly gone from the more populated parts of the world, while more people live in the denser population centers instead of out in the country; simply stating it like that would be sufficient to explain the narrower focus without excluding wolf-born completely. The ecological situation is.. well, it's really f-ing bad, isn't it? If Gaia is not already past the point of no return, she is very close. And the current generation knows it - and as terrible as it is to say this - fits like a glove to the game's premise.<br /> The 'loss of the wolf' is something that could be worked into the setting as a symbol for the losing war, and another point for players to rebel against. If the focus is more on humanity, then the antagonists should also be more human. As is evident, we do not need the help of supernatural evil to destroy our world. That's not to say that the spiritual side of the setting should vanish. Aside from pure game mechanics, it provides another possible anchor for players to ground themselves with.<br /> <br /> tldr; the setting progressions in W5 are not as much of a problem as the disappearance of narrative key elements that support the game's premise. In my opinion. </div> </div> </div>Seriously speaking, IMO just by the points above I can already think that the younger Garou are happy because the Garou nation fell, it seems more likely, even natural, literally lifted a weight from their shoulders and who cares what to solve it, after that W5 just seems more realistic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T04:51:10-07:00","id":1514823,"title":"","content":"I thought about this a bit, and a theme/unique trait that could maybe work is 'Dysphoria'. Looking for a place to belong, figuring out whether to embrace the wolf or man or both inside, finding personal ethics and convictions, and trying to become what you want to be. I haven't played Changeling, but I think that may be something of a theme there, so I'm not sure. It's at least the one most fitting thing I can think of for a young post-apocalyptic werewolf.<br /> <br /> That would make the Tribes more of 'what you want to do' and in line with W5 (as I understood the intention), where you find people with common interest. The pack would probably gain more importance as a social unit, as friends on a similar quest.<br /> There would need to be a strong motivating mechanic though, because dysphoria is a rung on the ladder to depression, and that's no fun to play. The game would certainly become more introvert / introspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T06:18:01-07:00","id":1514950,"title":"","content":"Honestly if I was given the task of writing W5 I would give both the players and ST's the tools to make whatever stories they like.<br /> <br /> If you want a coming of age story interspersed with ultra volince then you can, you want a tale of intergenerational conflict involving the pcs cleaning up they're forefathers mess you can do that, hell if you want to run a campaign around furry anime warriors battle against a comically evil corporation more power to you.<br /> <br /> The only narrative limitation I would set is that the game would take place in projet moon's city because is Underrated and it's less screwed up setting than world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 06-15-2023, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T22:51:13-07:00","id":1517140,"title":"","content":"So, there have been a few previews after I posted this. So here are my additional thoughts;<br /> <br /> -Controversial first: You can have pariah dog, dingo, coyote, jackal and all other types of canids that can breed with wolves and result in fertile offspring as shifter bases. Since the focus is on created werewolves vs born ones, there is a lot of variety among these garou.<br /> <br /> - Losing the wolf/human is HARD, it isn't simply losing willpower and rage, it requires the garou to basically spiritually subdue their unwanted half. Note that I said the <i>unwanted</i> half, there are homids who will choose to live as wolves to avoid the stress of the modern world and there are lupus who choose humanity due to its ease of survival.<br /> <br /> -Rage dice are not compulsory unless your Rage is greater than your willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T12:17:16-07:00","id":1517167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea#post1514713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To wit, a strong theme of W5 is balancing being a monster with your humanity, along with the monster species you are fighting a very dire war. You are forced to choose between joining the war or keeping in touch with your humanity.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea#post1514713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a lot of people who like Werewolves did not like WtA's wheels. W5 could have been a chance to focus on the cursed-type of werewolf.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, W5 seems to be a solution in search of a problem. Mechanics and lore already exist if players want to emphasize the &quot;personal horror&quot; aspect of the setting. It was just decided, for whatever reason, that &quot;savage horror&quot; was to be the theme and those aspects that dealt with the Garou as cursed creatures were neglected. There's no problem with that, as many players would find that distracting rather than fun. But if you wanted to emphasize that, most people probably only need 5-10 pages or so of guidance that could have been slipped into the Players Guide or Storytellers Handbook.<br /> <br /> (Please keep in mind I am ignorant of 99% of W5 and have avoided the W5 threads, so if I say something ignorant about W5, well it is just ignorance.)<br /> <br /> The two primary means are the Curse and Harano.<br /> <br /> The Curse has always been a way to emphasize the tragedy and cost of being Garou. And while low Rage Garou can often avoid the Curse entirely, there's always been the idea that it is easy for Garou to gain Rage and that Temporary Rage can always go above Permanent Rage. So even your one dot of Rage can experience this issue at some point.<br /> <br /> So if you want to emphasize a personal horror aspect that the werewolf is cursed, the ST just needs to work with the PC on what kind of things would cause the PC to gain Rage <i>when they would not normally want</i> any extra Rage (this is different from things which players would normally want to regain Rage, like in the presence of some blasphemous horror or their first wound in combat). Then if you want a touchstone mechanic, the ST and Player works together to provide touchstones that would eliminate this &quot;unwanted&quot; Rage.<br /> <br /> Harano would be similar. Have some kind of Harano tracker, perhaps adjusted by chronicle needs or tenets (if players don't want this at all, don't do it. Or limit its use only after the Garou hits a certain age or experiences a major personal loss, or based on Rank, so that you don't have young Garou succumbing to it). Detail what kind of losses they experience would fuel that (which could be tied back to the Curse and the lack of meaningful interaction with the world and thus isolation). Then work on how touchstones can alleviate the pain and send the track backwards.<br /> <br /> If you want, you can even tie both of these mechanics in some way to one's tribe (or lack thereof) as a result of the Totem's influence, spiritual correspondence, cultic devotion, etc. And maybe things like touchstones associated with the caern moot, or rituals/roleplay with the pack totem, can also affect these in a positive or negative way.<br /> <br /> Also make it a more viable option than a Ronin PC can be in the same gaming group as tribal PCs. A Ronin can still be outcast, and perhaps not technically a member of the pack and not have the Totem background, but they can still hang out with their fellow PCs but suffer social penalties with other Garou. Orient their Curse and Harano in a different way than the tribal PCs, so that there is a real distinction between them. You just need a slightly modified depiction of Ronin from canon, and various examples and guidance provided to the ST in order to do this. The different struggles between these character types can highlight another source of tragedy for the Garou.<br /> <br /> Want to show even more cursed elements? Instead of relegating the concept of Lunatics to Valkenburg Foundation and never mentioning them again, include that in the corebook, Rage books, and so on and explain how they are incorporated into the setting and offer things for PCs to do.<br /> <br /> The important thing is to make these kind of mechanics the servant to the ST and Players, and not their master. Use it when it is fun for the gaming group, and don't use it if it gets into the way of having fun. That way every gaming group can find their own sweet spot.<br /> <br /> I include and highlight a lot of these elements in my own chronicles, because I do like the idea of the more cinematic &quot;tragic&quot; werewolf. Because my players appreciate this, but don't themselves want to be sandbagged, I emphasize this more as an element for the NPCs and tailor my approach to any PCs based on what is fun for them to experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T12:37:13-07:00","id":1517168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1517167#post1517167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> To me, W5 seems to be a solution in search of a problem. Mechanics and lore already exist if players want to emphasize the &quot;personal horror&quot; aspect of the setting. It was just decided, for whatever reason, that &quot;savage horror&quot; was to be the theme and those aspects that dealt with the Garou as cursed creatures were neglected. There's no problem with that, as many players would find that distracting rather than fun. But if you wanted to emphasize that, most people probably only need 5-10 pages or so of guidance that could have been slipped into the Players Guide or Storytellers Handbook.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of fluff, W5 is going for the direction of independent garou over the Nation. And from what glimpses of approval I have seen on Twitter and Reddit, there are people wanting that.<br /> <br /> I mean, your idea is great and is one I've always loved to use. Especially Ronin and Lunatics.<br /> <br /> But given just HOW hard W5 has pushed the PCs away from the Nation and so much of the focus is on the personal horror, I'd say a purely ronin/lost cub/lunatic game would reflect it the best.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T01:43:16-07:00","id":1517200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1517168#post1517168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of fluff, W5 is going for the direction of independent garou over the Nation. And from what glimpses of approval I have seen on Twitter and Reddit, there are people wanting that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>imo reddit and twitter should be ignored when it comes to dialogue for a number of reasons. Twitter is a sad sad place full of stupid people with a very short word limit.<br /> <br /> I've seen the people posting this sort of thing but it's not clear they're a majority of outlook. For example the reddit traffic on wod seems to have dropped dramatically as the overall amount of criticism declined. This seems to imply more that people are walking away rather than coming around.<br /> its also worth noting that writting a game of werewolf the apocalypse for people who don't like it isn't a very good idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> also some of reddit and twitter takes are mind numbingly bad. &quot;Getting rid of Sabbat play is a neccissary evil because they might draw in gamergaters&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-05-2023, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T01:57:27-07:00","id":1517202,"title":"","content":"My own suggestions would be to create ambiguities on gaia, having differant tribes interpret her nature with differant aspects as well as having differant tribes focusing on differant aspects of the wyrm. For example the children of gaia would be more about addressing toxic social attitudes rather than enviromental destruction which would be more the domain of groups like the talons and territory orientated tribes.<br /> <br /> I'd also be tempted to follow revised I showing how the nation is growing and beginning to change gear in the face of defeat.<br /> <br /> Id definatly clean up the combat system to be robust abd dynamic.<br /> <br /> The final big change is id have maybe 3-5 wyrm tribes to ad a werewolf civil war aspect to the game.<br /> <br /> Nothing world changing but some solid steps","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T01:59:34-07:00","id":1517203,"title":"","content":"One question, I heard that in W5 the Garou condition will no longer be hereditary, it will be something that happens to some people without a specific explanation, something similar to mages and avatars from what I understand, does anyone know the veracity of this information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T02:03:10-07:00","id":1517204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1517202#post1517202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own suggestions would be to create ambiguities on gaia, having differant tribes interpret her nature with differant aspects as well as having differant tribes focusing on differant aspects of the wyrm. For example the children of gaia would be more about addressing toxic social attitudes rather than enviromental destruction which would be more the domain of groups like the talons and territory orientated tribes.<br /> <br /> I'd also be tempted to follow revised I showing how the nation is growing and beginning to change gear in the face of defeat.<br /> <br /> Id definatly clean up the combat system to be robust abd dynamic.<br /> <br /> The final big change is id have maybe 3-5 wyrm tribes to ad a werewolf civil war aspect to the game.<br /> <br /> Nothing world changing but some solid steps</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, kind of the BSD have it all covered in that regard, unless they've split and I don't know of a reason for that, except maybe if you want a tribe related to Weaver or Infernalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T02:21:09-07:00","id":1517205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1517204#post1517204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless they've split and I don't know of a reason for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually this exist in W:tA<br /> <br /> The <b><i>Silver Spiral</i> </b>is a seperate Silver Fang &quot;Camp&quot;; not actually a true house, but a generic designation to those among the Silver Fangs who have gone over to the Wyrm's side<br /> The <b>Eaters of The Dead</b> are not danced the Spiral, in a sense, could be worse than any Black Spiral Dancer<br /> The Child of Gaia geneticist Cernonous, has sought ways to restore the Bunyip... and brought them back. Or at least <i>something</i>. Those Bunyip, calling themselves the <b>Hollow Walkers</b>, forced their father to walk the Black Spiral and join them, but they are not Black Spiral Dancers<br /> Int the Apocalypse scentaroi where a tribes falls, the Shadow Lords not played too well with the Spirals, simply absorbed them, how Grandfather devoured Whippoorwill - and W20 Book of the Wyrm mentions the &quot;Fallen&quot; Lords are still Lords in a sense, and a Spiral shoudl be carefull around them<br /> <br /> The CyberDogs tried to machinize Gaia to make her more resilient against the Wyrm - basically fallen to the Weaver<br /> <br /> The Central American and Southern North American, i.e. South of Oklahoma, Black Furies experienced a curious Wyld Plague. The Metamorphic Plague was responsible for a growing number of male non-metis in Furies at large. The disease was far more likely to affect the infected's psyche. The plague altered a fundamental principle within the person dramatically, i.e. turns a 180 degree arc on it. Personalities, memories, and even gender can change.<br /> - some of the tribe tehcnicall fallen to thew Wyld","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T02:49:08-07:00","id":1517206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1517205#post1517205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually this exist in W:tA<br /> <br /> The <b><i>Silver Spiral</i> </b>is a seperate Silver Fang &quot;Camp&quot;; not actually a true house, but a generic designation to those among the Silver Fangs who have gone over to the Wyrm's side<br /> The <b>Eaters of The Dead</b> are not danced the Spiral, in a sense, could be worse than any Black Spiral Dancer<br /> The Child of Gaia geneticist Cernonous, has sought ways to restore the Bunyip... and brought them back. Or at least <i>something</i>. Those Bunyip, calling themselves the <b>Hollow Walkers</b>, forced their father to walk the Black Spiral and join them, but they are not Black Spiral Dancers<br /> Int the Apocalypse scentaroi where a tribes falls, the Shadow Lords not played too well with the Spirals, simply absorbed them, how Grandfather devoured Whippoorwill - and W20 Book of the Wyrm mentions the &quot;Fallen&quot; Lords are still Lords in a sense, and a Spiral shoudl be carefull around them<br /> <br /> The CyberDogs tried to machinize Gaia to make her more resilient against the Wyrm - basically fallen to the Weaver<br /> <br /> The Central American and Southern North American, i.e. South of Oklahoma, Black Furies experienced a curious Wyld Plague. The Metamorphic Plague was responsible for a growing number of male non-metis in Furies at large. The disease was far more likely to affect the infected's psyche. The plague altered a fundamental principle within the person dramatically, i.e. turns a 180 degree arc on it. Personalities, memories, and even gender can change.<br /> - some of the tribe tehcnicall fallen to thew Wyld</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen about fields that are like this and in fact they can be interesting antagonists, and there's a lot more I think, it could even show how each group interacts in the apocalyptic scenario, I just don't know if they're enough to call it a tribe, and some of them I I don't even know how they didn't dance the spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T03:12:40-07:00","id":1517207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1517206#post1517206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't know if they're enough to call it a tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tirbe could be...loosely interpreted<br /> The<b> Siberakh, </b>the <b>Skin Dancers </b>even the <b>Singing Dogs </b>are Tribes with distinct Totems, Sable, Minotaur and Bird of Paradise<br /> The <b>Boli Zouhisze</b> and the <b>Hakken </b>while part of the &quot;main tribe&quot; technically considered their own tribes on the East<br /> The <b>Kucha Ekundu </b>is a good question tho'<br /> <br /> But the first three? Tribes, yet I don't think they have members of the three digit numer<br /> Sure, the Silver Spiral, the Eaters abd the Hollow Walkers don't have a Totem/Patron of their own (or do they? My memories are a bit foggy) but still could be considered a sub-section, or a split section of the Black Spiral Dancers or outright their rivals in the case of the fallen Lords (or the followers of Susanowo or Typhon, it is a bit murky regarding those totems)<br /> <br /> So I think - but could be wrong - they could work as a split/additional Fallen Tribes even if just nominally Tribes in some cases<br /> <br /> Or at leats could have worked but W5 took another route<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T03:30:42-07:00","id":1517208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1517204#post1517204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, kind of the BSD have it all covered in that regard, unless they've split and I don't know of a reason for that, except maybe if you want a tribe related to Weaver or Infernalists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the idea is a larger scale conflict front rather than how spirals are used. Its more my personal taste. If I in charge I'd mostly keep the revised setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T03:46:49-07:00","id":1517209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514713-alternative-w5-idea?p=1517203#post1517203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question, I heard that in W5 the Garou condition will no longer be hereditary, it will be something that happens to some people without a specific explanation, something similar to mages and avatars from what I understand, does anyone know the veracity of this information?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed the case. Rather than hereditary, the way it works now is through the concept of &quot;Kin&quot; who are just random people who happen to qualify to experience the First Change at some point in their life (I always called it &quot;random&quot; because according to the previews no Garou knows how this process works). From the Lexicon in the introduction:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kin: A Werewolf who has not yet been accepted as Garou \u2014 a werewolf who doesn\u2019t yet know that they\u2019re a werewolf\u200b </div> </div> </div>And this gets tied into Kinseeking, one of the things listed in the Introduction under &quot;What do Werewolves do?&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of mysteries, werewolves must be forever vigilant for others of their kind who don\u2019t yet know what they are. Kinseeking Garou are always looking out for others of their kind, whether to mentor them in the ways of their pack or Patron Spirit, or to keep them out of the clutches of the so-called fallen tribes. Werewolves are few and far-between, and there\u2019s almost nothing so ruinous \u200bas the loss of kin-wolves to the extreme ideologies of wayward tribes or to the realities of being a werewolf with no knowledge of how to handle it.\u200b </div> </div> </div>As a concept, it's pretty close to an idea from WtF 1E actually where packs were battling each other over who gets to recruit the werewolf who had just undergone the First Change (2E doesn't have the same approach and it isn't described as this distinct activity anymore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}